safix::picker_needs_terminal

  × choosing needs a terminal, and there is none to offer one on. Nothing was
  │ decrypted.
  │ 
  │ A picker draws a list, reads single keystrokes, and redraws — so it needs
  │ /dev/tty and it needs to put it in raw mode. Where either is unavailable
  │ there
  │ is no reduced picker to fall back to: a list that cannot be moved through
  │ is a
  │ list, which is safix list, and a prompt that reads a line is not what was
  │ asked
  │ for. So this refuses rather than degrading.
  │ 
  │ Two ways on. Name the entry, which never needs a terminal and is what a
  │ pipeline wants:
  │ 
  │     safix view <name>
  │ 
  │ Or see what is there first, and then name it:
  │ 
  │     safix list [<user>]
